# Never normalise line endings. This repository is deliberately mixed: most sources are LF, but six
# files are committed with CRLF, and upstream is a Windows project that may add more. Without this,
# whether those six change depends on each contributor's core.autocrlf setting — so a checkout on one
# machine produces a diff on another, and a routine edit silently rewrites every line of a file.
#
# `-text` means "treat as binary for end-of-line purposes": git stores and checks out exactly the
# bytes committed, in both directions. Whatever a file already uses, it keeps.
#
# If a file's endings ever genuinely need changing, do it as its own commit so the diff is legible
# rather than hidden inside an unrelated change.
* -text
